- Google Maps Geolocation API (mapping) - location based on cell towers and WiFi signals.  
- Smart-IP-Geo-IP (mapping) - IP lookup service.  
- Telize (mapping) - IP geolocation.  
- Quova (mapping) - IP geolocation with comprehensive detail.  
- Bing Maps Locations - To get coordinates for a location from address or postal code.  
- Google Maps Geocoding - address lookup and reverse geocoding.

Since the app “triangulates the location of the outage” the IP geolocation APIs are most appropriate because the location of outage reporters can be deduced from their IPs or devices, then converted to geographical locations the power company can use. Google Maps Geolocation that uses mobile/Wi-Fi/cell data is also very useful if the app is mobile-based and the user allows access to GPS/location data.

